# AURION — environment overrides
#
# Nothing here is required: with no variables set the desk and the engine use
# the repository layout and bind to the loopback defaults in
# config/aurion.json. Copy this file to `.env` for your own notes — AURION
# does not read `.env` itself, so export the variables or pass them on the
# command line:
#
#   AURION_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/aurion node backend/src/index.js

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where AURION keeps state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything written at runtime — the access database, the JWT secret, the
# engine database, logs, exports, uploads, licence state. Point it at a volume
# or a per-user profile to keep the source tree clean. Honoured by both the
# Node desk and the Python engine.
#AURION_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/aurion

# Where config/aurion.json is read from and written to. The factory defaults
# always ship with the source tree, so a fresh directory bootstraps correctly.
#AURION_CONFIG_DIR=/etc/aurion

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Running behind a reverse proxy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default the desk sends `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and accepts CORS only from
# loopback — correct for a local application, fatal behind a proxy or inside
# an iframe. Name the hosts explicitly; there is no implicit relaxation.
#
# Extra CORS origins, comma-separated. "*" allows any (development only).
#AURION_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://desk.example.com

# Hosts allowed to frame the desk, comma-separated. Unset keeps DENY.
#AURION_FRAME_ANCESTORS=https://portal.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing — see store/keyserver/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#AURION_KEYSERVER_URL=https://your-keyserver
#AURION_STORE_URL=https://your-keyserver

# Ed25519 public key the engine verifies product keys against. The matching
# private key belongs on the key server and the owner machine ONLY.
#AXIASOFT_KEY_PUBLIC=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram status bot (read-only; optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provisioned from config/telegram.token — see config/telegram.token.example.
